\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Proposed pathways linking low precession and stronger boreal seasonality to DO recurrence. (a) A warmer Atlantic warm pool reduces moisture export to the Pacific; fresher water transported north increases stratification and initially weakens the AMOC, after which internal feedbacks can sustain oscillations \citep  {zhang2021direct}. Cyan ice sheets and white sea ice depict a schematic stadial background, with illustrative ice sheet margin inspired by \citet  {zhang2017abrupt}. (b) Thinner sea ice can favor earlier warming, while greater winter heat loss from open water can shorten the warm state \citep  {kuniyoshi2022effect}. The dashed arrow indicates a proposed lower subsurface-temperature threshold for sea-ice retreat \citep  {fohlmeister2023role}; the heat reservoir does not imply faster heat accumulation under low precession. The arrows summarize mechanisms operating at different stages of a cycle, rather than simultaneous changes.}}{13}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:orbital_mechanism}{{4}{13}{Proposed pathways linking low precession and stronger boreal seasonality to DO recurrence. (a) A warmer Atlantic warm pool reduces moisture export to the Pacific; fresher water transported north increases stratification and initially weakens the AMOC, after which internal feedbacks can sustain oscillations \citep {zhang2021direct}. Cyan ice sheets and white sea ice depict a schematic stadial background, with illustrative ice sheet margin inspired by \citet {zhang2017abrupt}. (b) Thinner sea ice can favor earlier warming, while greater winter heat loss from open water can shorten the warm state \citep {kuniyoshi2022effect}. The dashed arrow indicates a proposed lower subsurface-temperature threshold for sea-ice retreat \citep {fohlmeister2023role}; the heat reservoir does not imply faster heat accumulation under low precession. The arrows summarize mechanisms operating at different stages of a cycle, rather than simultaneous changes}{figure.caption.6}{}}
